Feature: As a billing coordinator, I want the system to automatically verify a patient’s insurance coverage and pre-authorize radiology tests before scheduling, so that delays and manual verification errors can be reduced.

  # Acceptance Criteria:
  # Given a patient is scheduled for a radiology test,
  # When the billing coordinator selects “Schedule Test”,
  # Then the system should verify insurance eligibility via API.
  # 
  # Given the test requires pre-authorization,
  # When the request is sent,
  # Then the system should store the authorization ID and approval date in the billing record.
  # 
  # Given a test is not covered,
  # When the result is received,
  # Then the system should notify both the coordinator and patient, and offer alternative payment options.
  # 
  # Priority: P1
  # Risk: Medium
  # Status: In Progress

  @Positive
  Scenario: TC-001 - Schedule covered radiology test with successful insurance eligibility verification
    Given Log in as billing coordinator
    When Navigate to patient record with valid insurance
    And Select a CT scan procedure
    And Click "Schedule Test" button
    # Test Data: Patient ID: 12345, Insurance: ABC Health, Procedure: CT Head
    Then System calls insurance eligibility API, receives coverage confirmation, and proceeds to scheduling without errors.

  @Positive
  Scenario: TC-002 - Schedule radiology test that requires pre‑authorization and store authorization details
    Given Log in as billing coordinator
    When Open patient record with insurance that mandates pre‑authorization
    And Select an MRI procedure
    And Click "Schedule Test"
    And Confirm pre‑authorization request when prompted
    # Test Data: Patient ID: 67890, Insurance: XYZ Care, Procedure: MRI Spine
    Then System sends pre‑authorization request via API, receives Authorization ID and approval date, and stores them in the billing record.

  @Negative
  Scenario: TC-003 - Attempt to schedule a test that is not covered by insurance
    Given Log in as billing coordinator
    When Open patient record with insurance lacking coverage for ultrasound
    And Select an Ultrasound procedure
    And Click "Schedule Test"
    # Test Data: Patient ID: 11223, Insurance: NoCover Inc., Procedure: Abdominal Ultrasound
    Then System receives non‑coverage response, displays notification to coordinator, sends email/SMS to patient, and presents alternative payment options.

  @Edge
  Scenario: TC-004 - Handle insurance API timeout during eligibility check
    Given Log in as billing coordinator
    When Open patient record
    And Select a CT scan
    And Click "Schedule Test"
    And Simulate insurance API timeout (no response within 10 seconds)
    Then System shows a timeout error message, allows coordinator to retry or cancel scheduling, and logs the incident.

  @Negative
  Scenario: TC-005 - Verify system behavior when insurance API returns malformed response
    Given Log in as billing coordinator
    When Open patient record
    And Select an MRI
    And Click "Schedule Test"
    And Mock insurance API to return invalid JSON
    Then System detects malformed response, logs error, displays user-friendly message, and prevents scheduling until a valid response is received.

  @Authorization
  Scenario: TC-006 - Schedule test for patient with expired insurance policy
    Given Log in as billing coordinator
    When Open patient record where insurance expiration date is past
    And Select an Ultrasound
    And Click "Schedule Test"
    # Test Data: Patient ID: 33445, Insurance: ExpireCo, Expiration: 2023-12-31
    Then System flags insurance as expired, notifies coordinator, and prevents scheduling until insurance is updated.

  @Edge
  Scenario: TC-007 - Concurrent scheduling attempts for the same patient and procedure
    Given Log in as billing coordinator on Workstation A
    When Open patient record and select MRI
    And Click "Schedule Test"
    And Simultaneously, on Workstation B, log in as another coordinator and repeat steps
    Then System handles concurrency, creates a single scheduling entry, and informs second user of existing pending request.

  @Non-Functional
  Scenario: TC-008 - Performance: Verify insurance eligibility API response time under load
    Given Generate 200 simultaneous "Schedule Test" actions for different patients
    When Measure time from click to receipt of eligibility response
    Then 95% of API calls return within 3 seconds, meeting performance SLA.

  @Authorization
  Scenario: TC-009 - Security: Ensure only authorized billing coordinators can trigger insurance verification
    Given Log in as a user with read‑only role
    When Attempt to access "Schedule Test" button for a patient
    And Observe UI controls
    Then Schedule Test button is disabled or hidden, and access is denied with appropriate authorization message.

  @Non-Functional
  Scenario: TC-010 - Validate audit log entry creation for insurance verification and pre‑authorization
    Given Log in as billing coordinator
    When Schedule a covered MRI that requires pre‑authorization
    And Complete the process
    And Query audit log for the patient record
    Then Audit log contains entries for eligibility check, pre‑authorization request, and storage of Authorization ID with timestamps.
